{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>At that time, etc. Hew for yourself.</b> Meaning: since the first tablets were the work of Elohim and not the work of Moses' hands, after the calf was made they were no longer fit for tablets such as those, and HaShem said to Moses that he should hew them from things that are attributed to him, to exclude what is attributed to El Elyon — those being the first ones." "He finished saying <b>and you shall make for yourself an ark of wood</b> — meaning, since they are the work of human hands they require a prepared place to be put in, something HaShem did not command to do for the first tablets. And the reason is that they stood on their own and did not need an ark apart from the ark that Bezalel made (Exodus 25:10). See what I have written at the verse ״וָאֶתְפֹּשׂ״ (Deuteronomy 9:17). And observe that it says <b>and you shall make for yourself</b>, to indicate to our way of understanding that since they are entirely yours, it is I who command you to make an ark."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:23.828222292Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}